===Mr. Psychic===
The southeast house belongs to a man known as Mr. Psychic. Speak to him, and after a moment of meditation, he hands out {{TM|29|Psychic}}.

===Silph Co.===
[[Silph Co.]] is open to the public, but a security guard explains that the elevator is not working due to some problem at the [[Kanto Power Plant|Power Plant]]. He feels bad that you wasted a visit, and gives out an [[Upgrade|Up-Grade]], one of the company's newest products that has not yet been released, as a souvenir.

===Magnet Train Station===
The [[Magnet Train]] station is located in the northwest part of the city. The train uses electricity and magnets to reach incredible speeds, but is also not running at the moment because of a service interruption at the [[Kanto Power Plant|Power Plant]].

===Fighting Dojo===
[[Saffron City]] is unique as the only city to have two Pokémon Gyms. The [[Fighting Dojo]] is located in the northeast neighborhood, next door to the [[Saffron Gym]]. The two clubs had once competed to determine which would become the city's one official Gym, and the {{t|Psychic}} Pokémon of Saffron Gym were victorious. A Black Belt informs visitors that the dojo's leader, [[Koichi|the Karate King]], is in [[Mt. Mortar|a cave]] in [[Johto]] for training.

====Meeting with Gym Leaders====
Having proven your worth by reaching the [[Hall of Fame]], you may now begin meeting with each [[Gym Leader]] in order to register his or her phone number in the [[Pokégear]]. Most numbers can only be obtained on a certain day and/or at a certain time, and some have additional requirements. 
