The [[Saffron Gym]] specializes in {{type|Psychic}} Pokémon. Psychic-type moves are super effective against {{t|Fighting}}- and {{type|Poison}} Pokémon, while Psychic-type Pokémon are weak to {{t|Bug}}-, {{t|Dark}}-, and {{type|Ghost}} moves.

The Gym uses {{DL|Saffron Gym|Generations I-IV|a series of warp tiles}} to confuse and disorient any challengers. Step on the tile near the entrance to reach the southeast room. To reach the Gym Leader by using as few warps as possible, continue by stepping on the northwest, southwest, and southwest tiles in the following rooms. This leads to the center room, where the [[Gym Leader]] awaits anyone up to the challenge.

Although [[Sabrina]] has only three Pokémon, they can become difficult to defeat if given the chance. She leads with her {{p|Espeon}}; both {{m|Psychic}} and {{m|Shadow Ball}} may lower the target's {{stat|Special Defense}}, letting it deal even more damage with subsequent attacks. {{m|Calm Mind}} boosts its {{stat|Special Attack}} and Special Defense, further increasing its damage output. {{p|Mr. Mime}}'s {{m|Mimic}} copies the target's most recent move, and {{m|Skill Swap}} lets it trade Abilities with the target. As {{a|Filter}} reduces damage sustained from super effective moves, using Skill Swap may actually backfire as it loses this protection. Her {{p|Alakazam}} cannot boost its power like Espeon can, but its high Special Attack makes it unnecessary. Both Psychic and {{m|Energy Ball}} may lower the target's Special Defense, and {{m|Reflect}} temporarily raises the team's physical {{stat|Defense}}, a common weakness of Psychic Pokémon.

